# Hosted-instrument evidence kept on disk for the release record and never staged: mailbox
# captures and QA identity dumps, production row censuses, CI job-log exports, a deployed-build
# Playwright report and a database probe. Each path is anchored to the repository root and named
# for the instrument that writes it, so the rule cannot also swallow a same-named source
# directory deeper in the tree. A .gitignore entry only prevents accidental staging; it is not
# access control on a shared host — `pnpm verify:hygiene` fails the release if a new root
# artifact appears without either being committed or being named here with a reason.
/p3c-red-baseline/
/prod-census/
/hosted-db-probe/
/live-playwright-report/
/6ab1d2b-ci-logs/
/c105edc-ci-logs/
